{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"9be4aad07c3d3e3bb0e8f931f24003055a06b27d3e7f4b69719ecfddd3ace59c","digest":{"component_or_area":"plan-review gate impact scoring model","key_entities":["src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py","src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify.py","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py","src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_verifier.md","src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_verifier_agentic.md","PlanSeverityAttrs.ac_unverifiable","ORACLE_GRADE01","UNDERSPECIFIED_ORACLE_CONTRIB","IMPACT_MODEL_VERSION","enrich_operator_attested","criteria_routing.json","docs/plan-review-gate.md"],"problem_keywords":["ac_unverifiable","hard-floor override","impact scoring","plan-review verification","oracle-kind classification","missing oracle","broken oracle","underspecified oracle","plan-v2 floor-driven blocks","severity grading"],"propositions":["35.5% of plan-v2 blocking findings (807/2271) are driven by the 0.85 hard floor that applies grade-blindly to any non-none ac_unverifiable severity, inflating block decisions for refinement demands that should not auto-block.","The ac_unverifiable axis must be split into three oracle-kind grades (missing_oracle, broken_oracle, underspecified_oracle) where missing/broken retain the 0.85 floor but underspecified oracle scores <= 0.55 to surface below the 0.60 blocking threshold.","PlanSeverityAttrs.ac_unverifiable must validate to a closed Literal set {none, underspecified_oracle, broken_oracle, missing_oracle} at write time, rejecting legacy or out-of-vocabulary grades in the verification parser.","The impact_plan scoring in decide.py must special-case ac_unverifiable out of both generic _SEV01 loops and apply oracle-grade-specific scoring via ORACLE_GRADE01 map, while the other three override axes (dod_uncertifiable, undecomposed, divergent_implementation) retain their ordinal vocabulary and any-non-none floor.","enrich_operator_attested must clear missing_oracle and underspecified_oracle findings upon operator attestation but never clear broken_oracle, since a factually wrong stated command cannot be cured by attestation.","IMPACT_MODEL_VERSION must bump from plan-v2 to plan-v3 in the same change; legacy plan-v2 sidecars persist and read as-is via version segmentation (no schema migration needed); forward-compatibility pinned by unit test that UNDERSPECIFIED_ORACLE_CONTRIB remains strictly below the minimum blocking threshold in criteria_routing.json."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785821384376435569,"uuid":"07f94ad8-672f-41e1-8b5d-3f2cd0aa3ecf"}